    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0243" n="143" xml:id="pg143"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">812.00/23663: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Vera Cruz</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Foster</hi>)<anchor n="6" xml:id="d142-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1920-04-23T12:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">April 23,
                                1920—noon</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Your April 20, 9 p.m.</p>
                <p>Navy Department is being asked whether it has available war vessel that could be
                    dispatched on reasonably short notice to Ports of Vera Cruz, Puerto México and
                    Frontera should emergency arise appearing to make such action advisable.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Colby</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d142-f1" n="6" type="source" xml:id="d142-f1-content">
                <p>The same, <hi rendition="#italic">mutatis mutandis</hi>, at 5 p.m., to the consul
                    at Frontera.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
